<title>USA: White House seeks U.N. review of Iraqi flight.</title>
<headline>White House seeks U.N. review of Iraqi flight.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The White House said on Thursday the United Nations should &quot;appropriately review&quot; Iraq's flying of pilgrims from Baghdad to Saudi Arabia in violation of U.N. economic sanctions.</p>
<p>Iraq flew 104 Moslem pilgrims to Saudi Arabia on Wednesday for the haj pilgrimage in an apparent attempt to use sensitive religious grounds to defy a United Nations air embargo.</p>
<p>&quot;This is a very important time on the calender for people of the Moslem faith and we have enormous respect for Islam, for those who wish to make the haj,&quot; White House Press Secretary Mike McCurry said.</p>
<p>&quot;At the same time Iraq does have obligations under the U.N. sanctions regime, and the U.N. should appropriately review this matter,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Asked what steps could be taken against Iraq, McCurry replied: &quot;That's a question for ... the sanctions commission at the U.N.&quot;</p>
</text>
